{"name":"Touch of Sun","hex":"#faf7e9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"touch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Primarily physical senses.\n To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.","The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Touch of the Sun (1956 film)","blocks":[{"text":"A Touch of the Sun is a 1956 British comedy film directed by Gordon Parry and starring Frankie Howerd, Ruby Murray and Dennis Price. It was written by Alfred Shaughnessy."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/A_Touch_of_the_Sun_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Touch_of_the_Sun_(1956_film)"},{"title":"Somatosensory system","blocks":[{"text":"The somatosensory system, or somatic sensory system, is a subset of the sensory nervous system. The main functions of the somatosensory system are the perception of external stimuli, the perception of internal stimuli, and the regulation of body position and balance (proprioception). It is believed to act as a pathway between the different sensory modalities within the body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Somatosensory_System.png/330px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Somatosensory_System.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somatosensory_system"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tactile_markings_stairs_for_visually_impaired.jpg/500px-Tactile_markings_stairs_for_visually_impaired.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tactile_markings_stairs_for_visually_impaired.jpg/500px-Tactile_markings_stairs_for_visually_impaired.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Touch is a crucial means of receiving information. This photo shows tactile markings identifying stairs for visually impaired people.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATactile_markings_stairs_for_visually_impaired.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png/500px-Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png/1280px-Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png/500px-Comprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This diagram linearly (unless otherwise mentioned) tracks the projections of all known structures that allow for touch to their relevant endpoints in the human brain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComprehensive_List_of_Relevant_Pathways_for_the_Somatosensory_System.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Gray759.png/330px-Gray759.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Gray759.png/330px-Gray759.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gray's Anatomy, figure 759: the sensory tract, showing the pathway (blue) up the spinal cord, through the somatosensory thalamus, to S1 (Brodmann areas 3, 1, and 2), S2, and BA7","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray759.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gray717.png/330px-Gray717.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gray717.png/330px-Gray717.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gray's Anatomy, figure 717: detail showing path adjacent to the insular cortex (marked insula in this figure), adjacent to S1, S2, and BA7","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray717.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Tickle.jpg/500px