luding the Sun. Distances are not to scale.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolar_System_True_Color_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/500px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/1280px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/500px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The photosphere is structured by convection cells referred to as granules.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHighest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_(NSF)_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg"}],"sounds":{"touch":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/En-us-touch.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fd/En-us-touch.ogg/En-us-touch.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-touch.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/db/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-touch.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-touch.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/db/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Bac